cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VGK Platform Security Stack - independent reverse-engineering reference"
message: "If you reference this material, cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "noel"
    alias: no33l
    website: "https://github.com/no33l"
year: 2026
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  Static, annotated reconstruction of the platform-integrity, measurement and
  attestation surface inside Riot Vanguard's kernel driver (vgk_rm.sys). Covers
  TPM command construction and PCR measurement, EK certificate handling, quote
  and credential flows, Secure Boot / UEFI / BCD readers, HVCI / VBS probes,
  composite hardware identifiers, debug-register paths, emulator and drift
  detection, crypto verification, evidence packets and self-guarding. Produced
  privately, handed to the vendor, published for informational use only.
keywords:
  - reverse engineering
  - windows kernel
  - platform security
  - tpm
  - attestation
  - secure boot
  - hvci
  - static analysis
license: other
repository-code: "https://github.com/no33l/vgk-platform-security"
